    "raw": "Given:\n- John plays 4 hours a day for 2 weeks (14 days).\n- After 2 weeks, he is 40% done with the game.\n- He then increases his playtime to 7 hours a day.\n\nFirst, calculate the total playtime in the first 2 weeks:\n\\[ 4 \\, \\text{hours/day} \\times 14 \\, \\text{days} = 56 \\, \\text{hours} \\]\n\nSince 56 hours of playtime corresponds to 40% of the game:\n\\[ 56 \\, \\text{hours} = 0.4 \\times \\text{Total game time} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total game time} = \\frac{56}{0.4} = 140 \\, \\text{hours} \\]\n\nNow, determine how much time is left to finish the game:\n\\[ 140 \\, \\text{hours} - 56 \\, \\text{hours} = 84 \\, \\text{hours} \\]\n\nWith the new playtime of 7 hours a day, calculate the number of days required to finish the remaining 84 hours:\n\\[ \\text{Days required} = \\frac{84 \\, \\text{hours}}{7 \\, \\text{hours/day}} = 12 \\, \\text{days} \\]\n\nFINAL: 12",
